   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
            <pb n="1" facs="Edgeworth_Princeton_1838-01-15_page01.jpg"/>
            <opener>
               <dateline>
                  <placeName ref="./Placeography.xml#Edgeworthstown_IE"/>Edgeworthstown <date
                     when="1816-08-04">Jan<hi rend="superscript">y</hi> 15<hi rend="superscript"
                        >h</hi> 1838.</date>
               </dateline>
            </opener>
            <p>It is wonderful to me to feel<lb/> that I have so much left to love<lb/> after having
               lost so much and <lb/> often as I feel this with <choice>
                  <orig>gra-<lb/> titude</orig>
                  <reg>gratitude</reg>
               </choice> to Heaven never did<lb/> I feel is more than on <choice>
                  <orig>read-<lb/> ing</orig>
                  <reg>reading</reg>
               </choice> your most kind letter my<lb/> dearest child, sister and friend<lb/>
            </p>
            <p>Well might my father say<lb/> Well did he prophecy, that<lb/> you dear <unclear><hi
                     rend="underline">little</hi></unclear> <persName ref="./Personography.xml#EdgeF3">Fanny</persName> as<lb/> then you were would be
               one<lb/> of the greatest blessings of my<lb/> life if prolonged to age -<lb/> God
               bless and preserve you<lb/> my dearest - not <hi rend="underline">merely</hi>
               <choice>
                  <orig>sel-<lb/> fishly</orig>
                  <reg>selfishly</reg>
               </choice> do I breathe this prayer<lb/> - <persName ref="./Personography.xml#EdgeL1"
                  >Lucys</persName> account &amp; <persName ref="./Personography.xml#WilsL1"
                  >Lestocks</persName> her<lb/> opinion of you are good and<lb/> for this I am
               thankful &amp; hopeful<lb/>
       
               <pb n="2" facs="Edgeworth_Princeton_1838-01-15_page02.jpg"/> I am glad you will not
               rack<lb/> yourself by driving or being<lb/> driven out till the weather is<lb/> finer
               and you stronger.<lb/>
            </p>
            <p>What a dreadful fire - The<lb/> 200 year old <placeName
                  ref="./Placeography.xml#Royal-Exchange_ENK">Greshams Exchange</placeName>
               <lb/> gone in a few hours - contents<lb/> of the iron chest and all!<lb/> I hope
                  <persName ref="./Personography.xml#WilsL1">Lestock</persName> and his
               partners<lb/> will not suffer by it <del>personall</del>
               <lb/> either in Insurance or any<lb/> other way - I do not like to write<lb/> to
               trouble him with inquiries or<lb/> condolence -- I trust we shall hear<lb/> from you
               all that concerns him<lb/> - He is to be with you on the 27<hi rend="superscript"
                  >h</hi>
               <lb/> I think - you need not plague<lb/> him with any question about<lb/> that old 13<add>2</add>
               draft - your mother<lb/> has had <persName ref="./Personography.xml#HoarC1"
                  >Hoare's</persName> account this<lb/> morning which has settled the<lb/> point no
               more about that -<lb/>
            </p>
            <p>I have gathered together all<lb/> the letters received since my last<lb/> Envoie
               which I think could<lb/> Interest you my dear &amp; if those<lb/>
            </p>
         </div>
      </body>
      <back/>
